{"t": 1794112537.6901217, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fees-float", "files": [{"content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\n\n\ndef fee(amount: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Processing fee: 1% of the amount, rounded to cents.\n\n    Per the card-network contract (PAY-88), fees must be computed on exact\n    decimal values and rounded HALF-UP, so 2.675 -> 2.68.  Using binary\n    floats with the built-in round() gives 2.67 because 2.675 is not exactly\n    representable, hence the Decimal conversion via str().\n    \"\"\"\n    exact = Decimal(str(amount)) * Decimal(\"0.01\") * Decimal(\"100\")\n    return float(exact.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n", "path": "payments/fees.py"}], "message": "Fix fee rounding: use Decimal HALF-UP per PAY-88\n\nThe float implementation of fee() used the built-in round(), which rounds\nthe binary float representation of 2.675 (2.67499999...) to 2.67 instead of\n2.68. Compute on exact decimal values and quantize with ROUND_HALF_UP as\nrequired by the card-network fee rounding contract (PAY-88).", "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
